OMINO MITSUAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI YASUHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AMANO, HIDEAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ENDO, SHOSUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJISATO, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMINO, MITSUAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, YASUHARU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A wafer stage (24) comprises a flat lower heater (38), upper and lower ceramic-metal members (40A, 40B) cooperating to sandwich the lower heater (38), and an electrostatic ceramic chuck (28) arranged on the upper side of the ceramic-metal member (40A) for holding a wafer (W) to be processed.  The ceramic-metal member (40A) and the electrostatic chuck (28) have substantially the same coefficient of linear expansion so that the difference in deformation between the two will not cause separation or damage to the electrostatic chuck (28).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un étage (24) de tranche comprenant un élément chauffant (38) inférieur, plat, des éléments (40A, 40B) céramique-métal supérieur et inférieur coopérant de façon à prendre en sandwich l'élément chauffant (38) inférieur, et un mandrin (28) céramique électrostatique placé sur la face supérieure de l'élément (40A) céramique-métal de façon à maintenir une tranche (W) devant être traitée. L'élément (40A) céramique-métal et le mandrin (28) électrostatique ont pratiquement le même coefficient de dilatation linéaire de sorte que la différence de déformation entre les deux ne provoque pas la séparation ou la détérioration du mandrin (28) électrostatique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>